2026-09-12 00:59:14,095 [INFO] excalibur.core.langfuse: [TOOL]: Write: {'file_path': '/tmp/rip_request.py', 'content': '#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport socket\nimport struct\n\ndef send_rip_request(target_ip):\n    """\n    Send a RIPv2 request packet to get routing table\n    RIP uses UDP port 520\n    """\n    # RIPv2 Request packet structure:\n    # Command (1 byte): 1 = Request\n    # Version (1 byte): 2 = RIPv2\n    # Must be zero (2 bytes): 0\n    # AFI (2 bytes): 0 for request all routes\n    # Route Tag (2 bytes): 0\n    # IP Address (4 bytes): 0\n    # Subnet Mask (4 bytes): 0\n    # Next Hop (4 bytes): 0\n    # Metric (4 bytes): 16 (infinity, means "send all routes")\n\n    rip_request = struct.pack(\'!BBHHHIIII\',\n        1,   # Command: Request\n        2,   # Version: RIPv2\n        0,   # Must be zero\n        0,   # AFI: 0 means request entire routing table\n        0,   # Route tag\n        0,   # IP Address\n        0,   # Subnet mask\n        0,   # Next hop\n        16   # Metric: 16 = infinity (request all routes)\n    )\n\n    try:\n        sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)\n        sock.settimeout(5)\n\n        # Send request to RIP port 520\n        sock.sendto(rip_request, (target_ip, 520))\n        print(f"Sent RIP request to {target_ip}:520")\n\n        # Try to receive response\n        try:\n            data, addr = sock.recvfrom(4096)\n            print(f"Received {len(data)} bytes from {addr}")\n            print(f"Raw data: {data.hex()}")\n\n            # Parse RIP response\n            if len(data) >= 4:\n                command, version = struct.unpack(\'!BB\', data[0:2])\n                print(f"Command: {command}, Version: {version}")\n\n                # Parse route entries (each entry is 20 bytes after 4-byte header)\n                offset = 4\n                route_num = 1\n                while offset + 20 <= len(data):\n                    afi, route_tag, ip, mask, next_hop, metric = struct.unpack(\'!HHIIII\', data[offset:offset+20])\n\n                    if afi == 2:  # Address Family: IP\n                        ip_str = socket.inet_ntoa(struct.pack(\'!I\', ip))\n                        mask_str = socket.inet_ntoa(struct.pack(\'!I\', mask))\n                        next_hop_str = socket.inet_ntoa(struct.pack(\'!I\', next_hop))\n                        print(f"\\nRoute {route_num}:")\n                        print(f"  Network: {ip_str}")\n                        print(f"  Netmask: {mask_str}")\n                        print(f"  Next Hop: {next_hop_str}")\n                        print(f"  Metric: {metric}")\n\n                    offset += 20\n                    route_num += 1\n\n        except socket.timeout:\n            print("No response received (timeout)")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"Error receiving response: {e}")\n\n        sock.close()\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f"Error: {e}")\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    send_rip_request("10.254.200.1")\n'}; start
2026-09-12 00:59:16,590 [INFO] excalibur.core.langfuse: [TOOL]: Bash: {'command': 'python3 /tmp/rip_request.py', 'description': 'Send RIP request to discover routes'}; start
